// Adopsi AFL - "Nggulung Duit Trading System v.1.0" ported from AmiBroker AFL to Pine Script v6
//
// WHAT THIS IS
// A port of the AFL chart template: the same signals (Buy / Sell / Flip / Flip+ / Flop), the same stop-and-
// reverse lines, the same IDX price ladder (tick size, ARA/ARB, BE/TP/SL), the same oscillators (SCAR/Kairi,
// Mansfield RSC vs IHSG, MFI with its divergence test), the same trend classification and the same ribbons.
//
// WHAT WAS DROPPED, AND WHY
//   - Backtest block (SetOption, PositionScore = Random() * MonteCarlo, ApplyStop): a Pine indicator cannot
//     size positions, and a PositionScore of Random() is not a ranking rule anyway. Port it to a strategy if
//     you want it, but note the scoring line would have to be replaced with something meaningful first.
//   - Exploration / AddColumn block: TradingView's equivalent is the Pine Screener, which is a different
//     script type. The same numbers are in the info table instead.
//   - GfxTextOut watermark: redrawn as a table (Pine has no GDI text), optional and off by default.
//   - Heikin-Ashi / MACD candle-colour block: it computed HaOpen/HaClose and several colour arrays that the
//     AFL never plots (every Plot call in that section is commented out). Nothing was lost by leaving it out.
//   - LineArray Fibonacci: kept, but see the note on repainting below.
//
// BUGS AND ODDITIES FOUND IN THE AFL (carried over only where they affect signals)
//   1. MFIPoint is always 0: MFI1d..MFI4d test `MFI(14) < 0`, and MFI is bounded 0..100. Same block in the
//      SCAR section tests `< 5` and in the RSC section `< 0`, so the three "point" counters are not comparable.
//      None of them is used by a signal, so this is dead code. Not ported.
//   2. ARBProsen uses the SAME tiers as ARA (35/25/20). The real ARB rule differs and has changed several
//      times. Ported faithfully, with the percentages exposed as inputs so you can set the current rule.
//   3. g60 = (EMA60*(2/4-1) - EMA60*(2/6-1)) / (2/4 - 2/6) simplifies EXACTLY to EMA(C,60). The arithmetic
//      cancels. Ported as a plain EMA(60) with this note.
//   4. Price rounding `X - (X % tick) + tick` rounds UP to the next tick, and adds a whole tick when X is
//      already on the grid, so every level sits one tick above its nominal value. Kept for fidelity, with a
//      switch ("Exact Tick Rounding") that floors instead.
//   5. The Fibonacci box is recomputed from the LAST 80 bars on every bar, so its levels move as new bars
//      arrive: historical readings of it are not what you would have seen at the time. Kept, default off.
//   6. `trendup`/`trendcolor` call ValueWhen(C, O<C) with the arguments in the wrong order. The result is
//      never plotted in the AFL, so it is not ported.
//   7. TP/SL percentages are measured from different anchors: TP from today's close, SL from YESTERDAY's
//      close. Ported as written; both anchors are visible in the table.
//   8. AVU vs AVUPlus: AVUPlus excludes BEDI_MFI (bearish MFI divergence), and AVU is what remains after
//      AVUPlus is excluded, so in practice "Flip" is the flip that carries a bearish divergence and "Flip+"
//      is the clean one. That is the opposite of what the names suggest. Ported as written.
//
// REPAINTING
//   Buy / Sell cross the 21-bar stop-and-reverse line, whose value depends on the highest / lowest CLOSE of
//   the last 21 bars including the current one. On a forming bar it can therefore move; on closed bars it is
//   fixed. Use "Once Per Bar Close" for alerts. Everything else reads confirmed data only.

//@version=6
indicator('Adopsi AFL', 'Adopsi AFL', overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 100, max_boxes_count = 50)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUTS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GROUP_LEVEL = 'IDX Price Ladder'
GROUP_SIGNAL = 'Signals'
GROUP_OSC = 'Oscillators'
GROUP_TREND = 'Trend & Rotation'
GROUP_VIS = 'Display'

legacyTicksInput = input.bool(true, 'Historical Tick Size Eras', group = GROUP_LEVEL, tooltip = 'The AFL carries three IDX tick ladders: before 6 Jan 2014, 6 Jan 2014 to 2 May 2016, and the current one. Off uses the current ladder for all history, which is what you want when you only trade recent data.')
exactTickInput = input.bool(false, 'Exact Tick Rounding', group = GROUP_LEVEL, tooltip = 'The AFL rounds every level with `X - (X % tick) + tick`, which rounds UP and adds a whole tick when X already sits on the grid. Off keeps that behaviour for fidelity; on floors to the grid instead.')
araTier1Input = input.float(35, 'ARA % (<200 / 200-5000 / >5000)', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'ara')
araTier2Input = input.float(25, '', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'ara')
araTier3Input = input.float(20, '', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'ara')
arbTier1Input = input.float(35, 'ARB % (<200 / 200-5000 / >5000)', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'arb', tooltip = 'The AFL uses the ARA tiers for ARB as well. BEI has changed the ARB rule several times, so set the current one here.')
arbTier2Input = input.float(25, '', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'arb')
arbTier3Input = input.float(20, '', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'arb')
be1Input = input.float(1.0, 'Buy Below % (BE1 / BE2)', minval = 0, maxval = 50, step = 0.5, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'be')
be2Input = input.float(4.0, '', minval = 0, maxval = 50, step = 0.5, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'be')
tp1Input = input.float(5.5, 'Target % (TP1 / TP2)', minval = 0.5, maxval = 100, step = 0.5, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'tp')
tp2Input = input.float(10.0, '', minval = 0.5, maxval = 100, step = 0.5, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'tp')
sl1Input = input.float(15.0, 'Stop % (SL1 / SL2)', minval = 0.5, maxval = 100, step = 0.5, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'sl', tooltip = 'Measured from YESTERDAY\'s close, as in the AFL, while the targets are measured from today\'s close.')
sl2Input = input.float(25.0, '', minval = 0.5, maxval = 100, step = 0.5, group = GROUP_LEVEL, inline = 'sl')

swingLongInput = input.int(21, 'Stop-and-Reverse Length (adon / tsl)', minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = GROUP_SIGNAL, inline = 'sar', tooltip = 'adon is the slow line the Buy / Sell crosses use; tsl is the fast line the Flip signals use and the source of the trigger and cut-loss prices.')
swingShortInput = input.int(5, '', minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = GROUP_SIGNAL, inline = 'sar')
showSignalLabelsInput = input.bool(true, 'Signal Labels', group = GROUP_SIGNAL, inline = 'siglbl', tooltip = 'Buy / TP / Flip / Flip+ / Flop text, as the AFL draws with PlotText. The arrows are separate.')
maxSignalLabelsInput = input.int(60, 'Keep Last', minval = 1, maxval = 500, group = GROUP_SIGNAL, inline = 'siglbl')
showArrowsInput = input.bool(true, 'Signal Arrows', group = GROUP_SIGNAL)

scarLengthInput = input.int(10, 'SCAR (Kairi) Length', minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = GROUP_OSC, inline = 'scar')
scarLevelInput = input.float(10, 'Level', minval = 1, maxval = 100, step = 1, group = GROUP_OSC, inline = 'scar', tooltip = 'SCAR = (close - MA) / MA x 100. Overbought at +level, oversold at -level.')
rscSymbolInput = input.symbol('IDX:COMPOSITE', 'RSC Benchmark', group = GROUP_OSC, tooltip = 'The AFL uses Foreign("IHSG","C"). IDX:COMPOSITE is the IHSG on TradingView.')
rscPeriodInput = input.int(52, 'RSC Period', minval = 2, maxval = 500, group = GROUP_OSC, inline = 'rsc')
rscLevelInput = input.float(2, 'Level', minval = 0.5, maxval = 50, step = 0.5, group = GROUP_OSC, inline = 'rsc', tooltip = 'Mansfield relative strength: ((close / benchmark) / its own average - 1) x 10.')
mfiLengthInput = input.int(14, 'MFI Length', minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = GROUP_OSC, inline = 'mfi')
mfiUpperInput = input.float(80, 'OB / OS', minval = 50, maxval = 100, step = 1, group = GROUP_OSC, inline = 'mfi')
mfiLowerInput = input.float(20, '', minval = 0, maxval = 50, step = 1, group = GROUP_OSC, inline = 'mfi')
showOscMarkersInput = input.bool(true, 'Oscillator Markers', group = GROUP_OSC, tooltip = 'SCAR triangles, MFI squares and stars, and the MFI divergence circles, at the same offsets the AFL uses.')

trendLongInput = input.int(150, 'Trend MA (long / mid / short)', minval = 2, maxval = 500, group = GROUP_TREND, inline = 'trend')
trendMidInput = input.int(70, '', minval = 2, maxval = 500, group = GROUP_TREND, inline = 'trend')
trendShortInput = input.int(14, '', minval = 2, maxval = 500, group = GROUP_TREND, inline = 'trend')
showRibbonsInput = input.bool(true, 'Ribbons (RRG bottom, MFI top)', group = GROUP_TREND, tooltip = 'The AFL draws these as own-scale candle ribbons. Pine has no own-scale overlay, so they are drawn as a strip of blocks at the bottom and top of the pane.')

showLinesInput = input.bool(true, 'Stop-and-Reverse Lines', group = GROUP_VIS)
showTableInput = input.bool(true, 'Info Table', group = GROUP_VIS, tooltip = 'Replaces the AFL Title block: price, volume value, 52-week range, position state, key levels, oscillator readings and the three trend horizons.')
tablePositionInput = input.string('Top Right', 'Table Position', options = ['Top Right', 'Top Left', 'Bottom Right', 'Bottom Left', 'Middle Right'], group = GROUP_VIS)
showWatermarkInput = input.bool(false, 'Watermark', group = GROUP_VIS, tooltip = 'The GfxTextOut block: ticker, price and company name in the middle of the chart. Off by default because it sits on top of the candles.')
showFibInput = input.bool(false, 'Fibonacci Box', group = GROUP_VIS, inline = 'fib', tooltip = 'Retracement levels of the last N bars. It is recomputed on every bar, so the levels move as the range moves; treat it as a live reading, not as history.')
fibLookbackInput = input.int(80, 'Bars', minval = 10, maxval = 500, group = GROUP_VIS, inline = 'fib')

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// IDX PRICE LADDER
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The three eras of the AFL, keyed on the same dates (DateNum 1140106 and 1160502).
int eraOne = timestamp('Asia/Jakarta', 2014, 1, 6, 0, 0)
int eraTwo = timestamp('Asia/Jakarta', 2016, 5, 2, 0, 0)

float tickLegacyOne = close < 200 ? 1 : close < 500 ? 5 : close < 2000 ? 10 : close < 5000 ? 25 : 50
float tickLegacyTwo = close < 500 ? 1 : close < 5000 ? 5 : 25
float tickCurrent = close < 200 ? 1 : close < 500 ? 2 : close < 2000 ? 5 : close < 5000 ? 10 : 25
float tickSize = not legacyTicksInput ? tickCurrent : time < eraOne ? tickLegacyOne : time < eraTwo ? tickLegacyTwo : tickCurrent

// @function            round a price onto the tick grid
// @returns             float
// The AFL form `X - (X % tick) + tick` rounds UP and overshoots by a full tick when X is already on the grid.
tickRound(float price) =>
    float floored = price - price % tickSize
    exactTickInput ? floored : floored + tickSize

float avgPrice = (open + high + low + close) / 4
float yesterdayClose = close[1]

float araPercent = close < 200 ? araTier1Input : close < 5000 ? araTier2Input : araTier3Input
float arbPercent = close < 200 ? arbTier1Input : close < 5000 ? arbTier2Input : arbTier3Input

float priceARA = tickRound(close + close * araPercent / 100)
float priceARB = tickRound(close - close * arbPercent / 100)
float priceBE1 = tickRound(avgPrice - avgPrice * be1Input / 100)
float priceBE2 = tickRound(avgPrice - avgPrice * be2Input / 100)
float priceTP1 = tickRound(close + close * tp1Input / 100)
float priceTP2 = tickRound(close + close * tp2Input / 100)
float priceSL1 = tickRound(close - yesterdayClose * sl1Input / 100)
float priceSL2 = tickRound(close - yesterdayClose * sl2Input / 100)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// VOLUME VALUE
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TraxDay is the value traded in billions of rupiah, the AFL's liquidity filter. On a daily chart TodayVolume is
// simply the bar's volume; intraday it accumulates from the start of the session, as `Sum(V, Bar_today)` does.
var float sessionVolume = 0.0
bool newSession = timeframe.isintraday ? ta.change(time('D')) != 0 : true
sessionVolume := newSession ? nz(volume) : sessionVolume + nz(volume)
float todayVolume = timeframe.isintraday ? sessionVolume : nz(volume)

float dailyVolumeEma = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, 'D', ta.ema(nz(volume), 20), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
float traxDay = todayVolume * hlc3 / 1e9
float trax20 = dailyVolumeEma * hlc3 / 1e9
float profOver20 = dailyVolumeEma > 0 ? (todayVolume - dailyVolumeEma) / dailyVolumeEma * 100 : 0.0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// OSCILLATORS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SCAR is Kairi: distance from a moving average in percent.
float scarMa = ta.sma(close, scarLengthInput)
float scar = scarMa != 0 ? (close - scarMa) / scarMa * 100 : na
bool scarOverbought = scar >= scarLevelInput
bool scarOversold = scar <= -scarLevelInput

// Mansfield relative strength against the benchmark. lookahead_off and the chart timeframe, so no leak.
float benchmarkClose = request.security(rscSymbolInput, timeframe.period, close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
float cociente = benchmarkClose > 0 ? close / benchmarkClose : na
float basePrice = ta.sma(cociente, rscPeriodInput)
float rsc = basePrice != 0 ? (cociente / basePrice - 1) * 10 : na

float mfi = ta.mfi(hlc3, mfiLengthInput)
bool mfiCrossUp = ta.crossover(mfi, mfiLowerInput)
bool mfiCrossDown = ta.crossunder(mfi, mfiUpperInput)

// The AFL's divergence test: a new price extreme that the MFI does not confirm, or an MFI extreme the price
// does not confirm. It compares against the running extreme of the same window rather than pivot to pivot.
bool bearishMfiDivergence = (close >= ta.highest(close, mfiLengthInput) and mfi < ta.highest(mfi, mfiLengthInput)) or (mfi <= ta.lowest(mfi, mfiLengthInput) and close > ta.lowest(close, mfiLengthInput))
bool bullishMfiDivergence = (close <= ta.lowest(close, mfiLengthInput) and mfi > ta.lowest(mfi, mfiLengthInput)) or (mfi >= ta.highest(mfi, mfiLengthInput) and close < ta.highest(close, mfiLengthInput))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// RELATIVE ROTATION QUADRANTS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rs is a 12/26 moving average spread rebased to 100; rm is the same transform applied to rs against its own
// 9-period average. The AFL's MA(rs, 1) is rs itself, so it is omitted here.
float rs1 = ta.sma(close, 12)
float rs2 = ta.sma(close, 26)
float rs = rs2 != 0 ? 100 * ((rs1 - rs2) / rs2 + 1) : na
float rmBase = ta.sma(rs, 9)
float rm = rmBase != 0 ? 100 * ((rs - rmBase) / rmBase + 1) : na

bool rrgLeading = rs > 100 and rm > 100
bool rrgWeakening = rs > 100 and rm < 100
bool rrgLagging = rs < 100 and rm < 100
bool rrgImproving = rs < 100 and rm > 100
bool rrgEntryUp = rrgImproving and rrgLagging[1] and profOver20 > 3
bool rrgExitDown = rrgWeakening and rrgLeading[1] and profOver20 <= 3

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TREND
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LinRegSlope(MA(C, n), 2) over two points is simply the one-bar change of that average.
float trendLong = ta.change(ta.sma(close, trendLongInput))
float trendMid = ta.change(ta.sma(close, trendMidInput))
float trendShort = ta.change(ta.sma(close, trendShortInput))

// @function            the AFL's trend wording for a slope
// @returns             string
trendWord(float slope) =>
    slope > 0 and slope < 0.3 ? 'Weak Up' : slope >= 0.3 and slope < 0.6 ? 'Medium Up' : slope >= 0.6 ? 'Strong Up' : slope < 0 and slope > -0.3 ? 'Weak Down' : slope <= -0.3 and slope > -0.6 ? 'Medium Down' : slope <= -0.6 ? 'Strong Down' : 'Sideways'

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STOP AND REVERSE LINES
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The AFL builds these with ValueWhen over a +1 / -1 state: while the state is up the line is the LOWEST close
// of the window (a trailing stop under price), and while it is down the line is the HIGHEST close (a trailing
// stop above price). Pine keeps the state in a var instead of ValueWhen.
// @function            state machine for one stop-and-reverse line
// @returns             [line value, previous state]
swingLine(int length) =>
    float upperBreak = ta.highest(close, length)[1]
    float lowerBreak = ta.lowest(close, length)[1]
    int signal = close > upperBreak ? 1 : close < lowerBreak ? -1 : 0
    var int state = 1
    if signal != 0
        state := signal
    [state == 1 ? ta.lowest(close, length) : ta.highest(close, length), state]

[adon, adonState] = swingLine(swingLongInput)
[tsl, tslState] = swingLine(swingShortInput)
// g60 in the AFL algebraically reduces to EMA(close, 60): the weights cancel exactly.
float g60 = ta.ema(close, 60)
float tslPrevious = tsl[1]

plot(showLinesInput ? adon : na, 'adon (slow SAR)', color = color.new(#66bb6a, 0), style = plot.style_stepline, linewidth = 2)
plot(showLinesInput ? tsl : na, 'tsl (fast SAR)', color = color.new(#9598a1, 0), style = plot.style_stepline, linewidth = 1)
plot(showLinesInput ? g60 : na, 'EMA 60', color = color.new(#42a5f5, 30), linewidth = 1)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNALS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bool buyLogic = ta.crossover(close, adon)
bool sellLogic = ta.crossunder(close, adon)

// Flop: stretched (SCAR) and confirmed by relative strength or money flow turning down.
bool flop = scarOverbought and (rsc >= rscLevelInput or mfi >= mfiUpperInput or mfiCrossDown)
// Flip+ is the clean flip; Flip is the same flip when a bearish MFI divergence is present (see note 8 above).
bool flipPlus = ta.crossover(close, tsl) and close > adon and not (flop or bearishMfiDivergence or mfi >= mfiUpperInput)
bool flip = ta.crossover(close, tsl) and close > adon and not (flop or mfi >= mfiUpperInput or flipPlus)

// ExRem: one Buy per position, one Sell per position.
var bool inLong = false
bool buySignal = buyLogic and not inLong
bool sellSignal = sellLogic and inLong
if buySignal
    inLong := true
if sellSignal
    inLong := false

// ValueWhen equivalents
var float buyPrice = na
var float sellPrice = na
var float triggerPrice = na
var int entryBarIndex = na
if buySignal
    buyPrice := tslPrevious
    entryBarIndex := bar_index
if sellSignal
    sellPrice := tslPrevious
if flip or flipPlus or flop
    triggerPrice := tslPrevious

int barsInPosition = inLong and not na(entryBarIndex) ? bar_index - entryBarIndex : na

float yearHigh = ta.highest(high, 240)
float yearLow = ta.lowest(low, 240)
float cutLoss = tsl - tickSize
float profitPercent = inLong and not na(buyPrice) and buyPrice != 0 ? (close - buyPrice) / buyPrice * 100 : na

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MARKERS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float markerAtr = nz(ta.atr(14))

plotshape(showArrowsInput and buySignal, title = 'Buy', style = shape.arrowup, location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(#ffffff, 0), size = size.small)
plotshape(showArrowsInput and sellSignal, title = 'Sell', style = shape.arrowdown, location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(#ffffff, 0), size = size.small)
plotshape(showArrowsInput and (flip or flipPlus), title = 'Flip / Flip+', style = shape.arrowup, location = location.belowbar, color = color.new(#ffeb3b, 0), size = size.tiny)

plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and scarOversold ? low - 1.6 * markerAtr : na, title = 'SCAR Oversold', style = shape.triangleup, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#26c6da, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and scarOverbought ? high + 1.6 * markerAtr : na, title = 'SCAR Overbought', style = shape.triangledown, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#f06292, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and mfi <= mfiLowerInput ? low - 0.7 * markerAtr : na, title = 'MFI Oversold', style = shape.square, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#4fc3f7, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and mfi >= mfiUpperInput ? high + 0.7 * markerAtr : na, title = 'MFI Overbought', style = shape.square, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#ffb74d, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and mfiCrossUp ? low - 0.35 * markerAtr : na, title = 'MFI Cross Up 20', style = shape.diamond, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#4fc3f7, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and mfiCrossDown ? high + 0.35 * markerAtr : na, title = 'MFI Cross Down 80', style = shape.diamond, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#ffb74d, 0), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and bullishMfiDivergence ? low - 1.0 * markerAtr : na, title = 'MFI Bullish Divergence', style = shape.circle, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#4fc3f7, 35), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showOscMarkersInput and bearishMfiDivergence ? high + 1.0 * markerAtr : na, title = 'MFI Bearish Divergence', style = shape.circle, location = location.absolute, color = color.new(#ffb74d, 35), size = size.tiny)

// Ribbons. Pine has no own-scale overlay plot, so the AFL's PlotOHLC ribbons become a strip of blocks pinned to
// the bottom (rotation quadrant) and the top (money flow state) of the pane.
color rrgColor = rrgLeading ? #26a69a : rrgImproving ? #42a5f5 : rrgLagging ? #ffd54f : #ef5350
color mfiRibbonColor = mfi < mfiLowerInput ? #26a69a : mfi > mfiUpperInput ? #ef5350 : mfiCrossDown ? #8d6e63 : mfiCrossUp ? #42a5f5 : #ffd54f
plotchar(showRibbonsInput, title = 'RRG Ribbon', char = '▬', location = location.bottom, color = color.new(rrgColor, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotchar(showRibbonsInput, title = 'MFI Ribbon', char = '▬', location = location.top, color = color.new(mfiRibbonColor, 20), size = size.tiny)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL LABELS  (the AFL's PlotText loop)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var array<label> signalLabels = array.new<label>()

// @function            add one signal label and keep the pool bounded
// @returns             void
addSignalLabel(string labelText, bool above, color labelColor) =>
    float labelPrice = above ? high + 1.1 * markerAtr : low - 1.1 * markerAtr
    signalLabels.push(label.new(bar_index, labelPrice, labelText, xloc.bar_index, yloc.price, color(na), above ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, labelColor, size.tiny))
    while signalLabels.size() > maxSignalLabelsInput
        label.delete(signalLabels.shift())

if showSignalLabelsInput
    if buySignal
        addSignalLabel('Buy ' + str.tostring(buyPrice, format.mintick), false, #66bb6a)
    if flipPlus
        addSignalLabel('Flip+', false, #ffd54f)
    if flip
        addSignalLabel('Flip', false, #b0bec5)
    if sellSignal
        addSignalLabel('TP', true, #ef5350)
    if flop
        addSignalLabel('Flop', true, #ce93d8)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FIBONACCI BOX
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Levels of the last N bars, redrawn on the last bar. The AFL loops over bars but only ever uses EndValue(), so
// the loop is redundant; the levels here are the same ones it ends up with.
var line fibLine0 = na
var line fibLine236 = na
var line fibLine382 = na
var line fibLine500 = na
var line fibLine618 = na
var line fibLine786 = na
var line fibLine100 = na

if showFibInput and barstate.islast
    float fibLow = ta.lowest(low, fibLookbackInput)
    float fibHigh = ta.highest(high, fibLookbackInput)
    float fibRange = fibHigh - fibLow
    int fibLeft = bar_index - fibLookbackInput + 1
    int fibMid = bar_index - int(fibLookbackInput / 2)

    line.delete(fibLine0)
    line.delete(fibLine236)
    line.delete(fibLine382)
    line.delete(fibLine500)
    line.delete(fibLine618)
    line.delete(fibLine786)
    line.delete(fibLine100)

    fibLine0 := line.new(fibLeft, fibLow, bar_index, fibLow, xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(#9598a1, 40), style = line.style_dotted)
    fibLine100 := line.new(fibLeft, fibHigh, bar_index, fibHigh, xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(#9598a1, 40), style = line.style_dotted)
    fibLine236 := line.new(fibMid, fibLow + fibRange * 0.236, bar_index, fibLow + fibRange * 0.236, xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(#9598a1, 70), style = line.style_dotted)
    fibLine382 := line.new(fibMid, fibLow + fibRange * 0.382, bar_index, fibLow + fibRange * 0.382, xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(#9598a1, 70), style = line.style_dotted)
    fibLine500 := line.new(fibMid, fibLow + fibRange * 0.5, bar_index, fibLow + fibRange * 0.5, xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(#9598a1, 55), style = line.style_dotted)
    fibLine618 := line.new(fibMid, fibLow + fibRange * 0.618, bar_index, fibLow + fibRange * 0.618, xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(#9598a1, 70), style = line.style_dotted)
    fibLine786 := line.new(fibMid, fibLow + fibRange * 0.786, bar_index, fibLow + fibRange * 0.786, xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(#9598a1, 70), style = line.style_dotted)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INFO TABLE  (the AFL Title block)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
string tablePosition = tablePositionInput == 'Top Right' ? position.top_right : tablePositionInput == 'Top Left' ? position.top_left : tablePositionInput == 'Bottom Right' ? position.bottom_right : tablePositionInput == 'Bottom Left' ? position.bottom_left : position.middle_right

var table infoTable = table.new(tablePosition, 2, 14, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(#9598a1, 70), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(#9598a1, 70))

// @function            one table row
// @returns             void
infoRow(int row, string label, string value, color valueColor) =>
    infoTable.cell(0, row, label, text_color = color.new(chart.fg_color, 35), text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left)
    infoTable.cell(1, row, value, text_color = valueColor, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)

if showTableInput and barstate.islast
    color neutralColor = chart.fg_color
    color upColor = #26a69a
    color downColor = #ef5350

    string stateText = inLong ? 'LONG since ' + str.tostring(barsInPosition) + ' bars' : 'FLAT'
    string mfiState = mfi < mfiLowerInput ? 'Oversold' : mfi >= mfiUpperInput ? 'Overbought' : 'Neutral'
    string rscState = rsc <= -rscLevelInput ? 'Oversold' : rsc >= rscLevelInput ? 'Overbought' : 'Neutral'
    string scarState = scar <= -scarLevelInput ? 'Oversold' : scar >= scarLevelInput ? 'Overbought' : 'Neutral'
    string rrgState = rrgLeading ? 'Leading' : rrgWeakening ? 'Weakening' : rrgLagging ? 'Lagging' : 'Improving'

    infoTable.cell(0, 0, syminfo.ticker, text_color = neutralColor, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    infoTable.cell(1, 0, str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + '  ' + str.tostring(nz(ta.roc(close, 1)), '0.00') + '%', text_color = close >= nz(close[1]) ? upColor : downColor, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_right)

    infoRow(1, 'Position', stateText, inLong ? upColor : neutralColor)
    infoRow(2, 'Profit', na(profitPercent) ? '-' : str.tostring(profitPercent, '0.00') + '%', na(profitPercent) ? neutralColor : profitPercent >= 0 ? upColor : downColor)
    infoRow(3, 'Trx today', str.tostring(traxDay, '0.00') + ' B  (' + str.tostring(profOver20, '0') + '% vs 20d)', profOver20 > 0 ? upColor : neutralColor)
    infoRow(4, 'Key levels', 'adon ' + str.tostring(adon, format.mintick) + ' | tsl ' + str.tostring(tsl, format.mintick), neutralColor)
    infoRow(5, 'Buy / Avg down', str.tostring(priceBE1, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(priceBE2, format.mintick), neutralColor)
    infoRow(6, 'TP1 / TP2', str.tostring(priceTP1, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(priceTP2, format.mintick), upColor)
    infoRow(7, 'Cut loss / SL1', str.tostring(cutLoss, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(priceSL1, format.mintick), downColor)
    infoRow(8, 'ARA / ARB', str.tostring(priceARA, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(priceARB, format.mintick), neutralColor)
    infoRow(9, '52w range', str.tostring(yearLow, format.mintick) + ' - ' + str.tostring(yearHigh, format.mintick), neutralColor)
    infoRow(10, 'MFI / RSC / SCAR', str.tostring(mfi, '0.0') + ' ' + mfiState + ' | ' + str.tostring(rsc, '0.00') + ' ' + rscState + ' | ' + str.tostring(scar, '0.0') + ' ' + scarState, neutralColor)
    infoRow(11, 'Rotation', rrgState + (rrgEntryUp ? '  (entry)' : rrgExitDown ? '  (exit)' : ''), rrgLeading or rrgImproving ? upColor : downColor)
    infoRow(12, 'Trend S/M/L', trendWord(trendShort) + ' | ' + trendWord(trendMid) + ' | ' + trendWord(trendLong), trendShort > 0 ? upColor : downColor)
    infoRow(13, 'Tick size', str.tostring(tickSize, '0'), neutralColor)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WATERMARK  (the GfxTextOut block)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table watermarkTable = table.new(position.middle_center, 1, 3)

if showWatermarkInput and barstate.islast
    color watermarkColor = close > open ? color.new(#26a69a, 55) : close < open ? color.new(#ef5350, 55) : color.new(#9598a1, 55)
    watermarkTable.cell(0, 0, str.tostring(close, format.mintick), text_color = watermarkColor, text_size = size.large)
    watermarkTable.cell(0, 1, syminfo.ticker, text_color = watermarkColor, text_size = size.huge)
    watermarkTable.cell(0, 2, syminfo.description, text_color = color.new(#9598a1, 60), text_size = size.normal)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ALERTS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Use "Once Per Bar Close": the stop-and-reverse lines can still move inside a forming bar.
alertcondition(buySignal, 'Buy', 'Close crossed above the slow stop-and-reverse line')
alertcondition(sellSignal, 'Sell / TP', 'Close crossed below the slow stop-and-reverse line')
alertcondition(flipPlus, 'Flip+', 'Clean flip: close crossed the fast line above the slow line')
alertcondition(flip, 'Flip', 'Flip with a bearish MFI divergence present')
alertcondition(flop, 'Flop', 'Stretched (SCAR) with relative strength or money flow turning down')
alertcondition(rrgEntryUp, 'Rotation Entry', 'Rotation moved from lagging to improving on rising volume')
alertcondition(rrgExitDown, 'Rotation Exit', 'Rotation moved from leading to weakening on falling volume')
